{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2103","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2103","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2103\",\"parent_revision\":\"4af968058fa9632c49c521bc72661001942ac8474ad33ddeeeffbb7078de7d08\",\"root_revision\":\"4af968058fa9632c49c521bc72661001942ac8474ad33ddeeeffbb7078de7d08\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add vague-brief fallback to research-curator and skill-research-process \u2014 generate n differentiated alternatives in parallel for user selection** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md \u2014 pattern: Design Direction Advisor (Fallback Mode)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: READY \u2014 2026-05-05\\n\\n**Decision**: READY \u2014 all previously MISSING conditions are now resolved. Implementation can begin.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen the orchestrator-facing skills `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` and `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md` receive a vague brief (URL with no clear category, generic skill description like \\\"make a research thing\\\", no resource name in the prompt), the workflow proceeds with the agent's best inference \u2014 there is no branch in either skill's mermaid graph that detects underspecification and stops to surface differentiated alternatives. Grep of `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/` for `vague brief`, `fallback mode`, `parallel alternatives`, or `differentiated direction` returns zero matches. As a result, ambiguous prompts are answered with a single best-guess output, and the user only discovers the misalignment after the work is done \u2014 when the iteration cost is highest.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAdd a Vague Brief Detector to `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` mode-routing flowchart and `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md` Stage 1. The detector evaluates an explicit set of conditions (e.g., URL is a homepage with no resource name; skill name is a non-noun phrase like \\\"do research on AI\\\"; no version/identifier in the prompt). When ANY condition matches, the skill enters Fallback mode and spawns 3 parallel `@research-curator` (or `@general-purpose`) agents, each scoped to a different interpretation of the brief. The orchestrator collects 3 brief 5-bullet summaries, presents them to the user with labeled differentiation axes, and waits for selection before continuing into the main workflow.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` contains a mermaid node labeled \\\"Vague Brief Detector\\\" with explicit branch conditions and a \\\"Fallback \u2014 spawn N parallel alternative agents\\\" branch. Running the skill with input `\\\"research AI tools\\\"` (no URL) causes the orchestrator to spawn N parallel agents and present N differentiated summaries before any entry is written. The skill defines the trigger conditions explicitly so agents can evaluate them without subjective judgement.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Conditions Verified\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence/Basis |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Trigger conditions \u2014 research-curator | AVAILABLE | Item enumerates 3 evaluable conditions: homepage URL with no resource name; non-noun phrase; no version/identifier. Confirmed against current SKILL.md mode-routing flowchart. |\\n| Trigger conditions \u2014 skill-research-process Stage 1 | MISSING | Item says \\\"same conditions applied to the argument\\\" but research-curator conditions are URL-based; skill-research-process takes a library name, not a URL. Conditions for the library-name case are not enumerated. |\\n| Canonical value of N | MISSING | Title says \\\"N\\\", target state says \\\"3\\\", source pattern (huashu-design.md \u00a74, lines 60-66) says \\\"3+\\\". AC #6 requires a specific integer. No stakeholder decision recorded. |\\n| User-selection wait mechanism | MISSING | Listed in Questions for Human as unanswered. Three candidates named but none selected. |\\n| Source pattern alignment | AVAILABLE | huashu-design.md lines 60-66 confirmed: trigger when brief too vague, 3 directions in parallel, user selects one, continues into main workflow. Minor gap: \\\"5-bullet summaries\\\" phrase comes from item description, not source \u2014 source describes direction cards with school/gestalt/designer. |\\n| Parallel agent output format | MISSING | Item says \\\"5-bullet summaries\\\"; source says \\\"flagship works, gestalt keywords, representative designer\\\" (different format). Agent tool prompts cannot be authored without knowing which format applies. |\\n| Insert point \u2014 research-curator | AVAILABLE | SKILL.md read in full (lines 26-38). Q3 terminal node at line 38 routes to Default. Vague Brief Detector diamond inserts between Q3 and Default. Confirmed. |\\n| Insert point \u2014 skill-research-process Stage 1 | DERIVABLE | Stage 1 (lines 41-57) has no entry-point flowchart \u2014 uses prose numbered steps. Detector must be inserted before Step 1. Form (Mermaid vs. prose) is a design decision not yet made. |\\n| /plugin-creator:skill-creator pre-condition | AVAILABLE | CLAUDE.md activation trigger confirmed: activate before any SKILL.md modification. Process gate, not information gap. |\\n| No downstream agent/script changes | DERIVABLE | @research-curator agents follow their prompt. If fallback prompt specifies output format, no agent file changes needed. Medium confidence \u2014 requires confirmation that agents are not constrained by their own SKILL.md to a specific output structure. |\\n| Clear bypass path for unambiguous inputs | AVAILABLE | AC #5 explicit. Insert-point analysis confirms: Q3 \u2192 clear-URL branch \u2192 existing Default (unchanged); Q3 \u2192 vague branch \u2192 Vague Brief Detector. Non-regression path is structurally sound. |\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resolved Design Decisions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **N**: Configurable via `--alternatives N` (default 3). Flowchart documents the default; argument overrides it.\\n- **skill-research-process vague conditions**: argument is generic category word (not a specific tool/library name) OR verb phrase. Version absence alone is not vague.\\n- **User-selection**: AskUserQuestion tool \u2014 blocks with numbered choice prompt, waits for user reply before continuing.\\n- **Card format**: Huashu-style direction card adapted for research: interpretation name + rationale (why this reading fits the brief) + research scope (3\u20134 concrete items) + keywords (3\u20135).\\n- **skill-research-process detector form**: prose decision block before Step 1 (no Mermaid in Stage 1).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Missing Inputs Required Before Implementation\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**[N value \u2014 blocking AC #6]**\\n- What is the canonical integer value for N? Is 3 confirmed, or is N configurable via a skill argument (e.g., `--alternatives 3`)? AC #6 states N must be a specific integer in the flowchart \u2014 it cannot remain a variable at implementation time.\\n\\n**[Trigger conditions for skill-research-process Stage 1 \u2014 blocking Stage 1 authoring]**\\n- research-curator conditions reference URL detection. skill-research-process takes a `<tool-or-library-name>` argument (no URL). Which evaluable conditions classify a library name as vague?\\n  - Candidate A: single generic word with no domain specificity (e.g., \\\"AI\\\", \\\"tools\\\", \\\"design\\\")\\n  - Candidate B: argument is a verb phrase rather than a noun (e.g., \\\"do research on AI\\\")\\n  - Candidate C: argument has no version identifier or qualifier\\n  Which apply? Are there additional conditions?\\n\\n**[User-selection wait mechanism \u2014 blocking orchestrator control-flow design]**\\n- How should the orchestrator present N alternatives and wait for user selection?\\n  - Option 1: Numbered blocking prompt (\\\"1) \u2026 2) \u2026 3) \u2026 Enter number:\\\") \u2014 orchestrator halts until user responds\\n  - Option 2: Inline labeled question \u2014 present summaries, ask user to reply with choice\\n  - Option 3: Other\\n\\n**[Parallel agent output format \u2014 blocking Agent tool prompt authoring]**\\n- Item description says \\\"5-bullet summaries\\\"; source pattern (huashu-design.md \u00a74) says \\\"flagship works, gestalt keywords, representative designer\\\" (direction card format). Which applies?\\n  - Option A: 5 bullets describing the research interpretation scope\\n  - Option B: Huashu-style direction card (school/gestalt/designer)\\n  - Option C: Custom format (specify)\\n\\n**[skill-research-process Stage 1 detector form \u2014 minor, can be decided at implementation time]**\\n- Stage 1 uses prose numbered steps, not Mermaid. Should the detector be: (a) a new Mermaid flowchart block before Step 1, or (b) a prose decision block? This can be decided by the implementing agent if stakeholder has no preference.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Approved Conditions Derivable Confirm Early In Implementation\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Insert point in research-curator: Q3 terminal \u2192 insert Vague Brief Detector diamond \u2192 existing Default branch (bypass path)\\n- No @research-curator agent file changes required if fallback prompt specifies output format explicitly\\n- /plugin-creator:skill-creator must be activated as first action before any SKILL.md edit\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Ambiguous prompts currently produce single best-guess output discovered to be wrong only after the full research workflow completes. Iteration cost at that point is high. Pattern is validated in the Huashu Design source and the fix is contained to two SKILL.md files.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Users who give vague research briefs from getting misaligned output silently\\n- Bottleneck: The `research-curator` default mode and `skill-research-process` Stage 1 are the only entry points \u2014 both must be updated to close the gap\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- User discovers misalignment at lowest-cost point (before any research work executes)\\n- Parallel alternative summaries give the user a concrete vocabulary for describing what they want\\n- Pattern is already validated in the codebase (Huashu Design Direction Advisor); no novel design needed\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a user invokes `/research-curator` with a vague input (no URL, generic description, non-noun phrase, no version identifier), the skill detects the condition and presents N differentiated interpretations of the brief as short summaries before spawning any research agents. The user selects one interpretation and the main workflow continues from that selection. Unambiguous inputs bypass the detector entirely with no change to existing behavior.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nBoth target SKILL.md files contain a Vague Brief Detector node in their entry-point flowchart. The detector evaluates a named, evaluable set of conditions \u2014 no subjective inference required. When triggered, it spawns N parallel agents (each scoped to a different interpretation), collects their short summaries, presents them to the user with labeled differentiation axes, and waits for a selection signal before continuing. The trigger conditions are explicit enough that an agent can evaluate them without human interpretation.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` mode-routing flowchart contains a Mermaid node labeled \\\"Vague Brief Detector\\\" with explicit, enumerated trigger conditions as branch labels \u2014 not subjective descriptions\\n2. The detector has a `Fallback` branch that spawns N parallel agents and a `Clear` branch that routes to the existing Q3/Default path unchanged\\n3. `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md` Stage 1 contains the equivalent detector before the `Initialize skill directory` step\\n4. Running either skill with input `\\\"research AI tools\\\"` (no URL, non-noun phrase) causes N parallel agents to spawn and N differentiated summaries to be presented to the user before any entry file is written or any category directory is initialized\\n5. Running either skill with a clear URL and resource name (`https://github.com/owner/repo`) bypasses the detector and follows the existing flow with no observable change\\n6. N is set to a specific integer (not a variable) and documented explicitly in the flowchart \u2014 the item context and source pattern both point toward 3\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What is the canonical value of N? The item title uses \\\"N\\\", the target state specifies \\\"3\\\", the source pattern (Huashu Design) uses \\\"3+\\\". Is 3 the intended default, or should N be configurable via an argument?\\n- What are the trigger conditions for `skill-research-process` Stage 1? The `research-curator` conditions are enumerated (homepage URL with no resource name; non-noun phrase; no version/identifier). Should `skill-research-process` use the same conditions applied to the `<tool-or-library-name>` argument?\\n- What is the user-selection wait mechanism? Should the orchestrator emit a blocking numbered-choice prompt (`1) Direction A  2) Direction B  3) Direction C \u2014 Enter number:`) and halt, or is a different interaction pattern expected?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Skill | /research-curator |\\n| Skill | /skill-research-process |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:skill-creator (required before SKILL.md modification) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md \u00a74 \u2014 Design Direction Advisor Fallback Mode (source pattern: 3 parallel agents, different interpretations, user selects one) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md \u2014 mode-routing flowchart (insert point: Q3 terminal branch, line ~38) |\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md \u2014 Stage 1 (insert point: before \\\"Initialize skill directory\\\" step) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained SKILL.md edits; no downstream agent or script changes required)\\n- Blocks: None identified; no backlog items depend on vague-brief detection being absent\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- N value must be decided before implementation (currently ambiguous between title and description)\\n- Trigger conditions for `skill-research-process` not yet enumerated \u2014 must be confirmed or derived before writing the Stage 1 detector\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Two SKILL.md files require Mermaid flowchart edits (insert one decision diamond with two branches into each). No code, no new agents, no scripts. Source pattern is fully documented and validated in `huashu-design.md`. Primary effort is `/plugin-creator:skill-creator` activation, Mermaid authoring, and linting.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:96a9584c064535b4e16c126ef4207746 -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"447364693c9c07026b50fe7d451137051101df7978d753748391a14550ecdc12\",\"comment_